<header><p class="st-kicker">colony · Mesoamerica and the Caribbean</p><h1 class="st-title">Colony of Barbados</h1><p class="st-meta">1627 CE – 1966 CE · capital Bridgetown</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">England's richest early colony, where the sugar revolution and its slave society took shape, governed by Britain until independence in 1966.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>English settlers financed by the merchant <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-courteen">William Courteen</a> landed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holetown">Holetown</a> in 1627 on the uninhabited island. Early colonists grew tobacco and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> with indentured servants, and an elected <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-assembly-of-barbados">House of Assembly</a> was established in 1639, one of the oldest legislatures in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/americas">Americas</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>In the 1640s planters turned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sugar-plantation">sugar</a>, and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/barbados">Barbados</a> became the model plantation colony, with enslaved Africans soon forming the large majority. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barbados-slave-code">Barbados Slave Code</a> of 1661 influenced other English colonies. After Bussa's rebellion in 1816 and emancipation in 1834-38, a planter elite still dominated. The 1937 riots led to labour reforms under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/grantley-adams">Grantley Adams</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/barbados">Barbados</a> gained universal suffrage in 1951, joined the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/west-indies-federation">West Indies Federation</a> in 1958-62 and became the independent state of Barbados on 30 November 1966 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/errol-barrow">Errol Barrow</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="colony, 1627 CE – 1966 CE"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 64 H80 L70 78 H30 Z"/><path d="M50 64 V18"/><path d="M50 22 L72 56 H50"/><path d="M50 28 L32 56 H50"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">colony</p><p class="st-emblem-reg